WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.970
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.750
JOHN COATES: Lawyers and negotiate
deals and manage lawsuits involving

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.520
billions of dollars each year.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.548
To do that, they need more
than purely legal expertise.

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:13.340
KENNETH FEINBERG: If
you don't know numbers

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:19.670
and you can't deal with concepts like
economic loss and likelihood of income

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:24.680
in the future, you'll find yourself
sort of at sea without a compass.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.710
JOHN COATES: You need a fundamental
understanding of finance,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.860
how to read financial
statements, how to analyze them,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.030
and how to use financial concepts
to value a business, or a patent,

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.740
or a marital estate.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:42.620
You need more than law to help a
client even decide whether to sue.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.980
BALA DHARAN: Lawyers cannot
leave accounting, finance,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.540
and valuation to a finance
team or outside experts.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.820
Through examples of valuation
disputes and presentations

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.060
from real-world
practitioners, this course

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.950
will teach you how to interpret
and use financial data,

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.610
make a business case
for a deal or a lawsuit,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:14.930
and know when and how experts can
support or undermine your work.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.630
JOHN COATES: Based on an essential
course at Harvard Law School,

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:22.258
this course is one of the few available
at the intersection of law and finance.

00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:25.050
PATRICIA LAUCELLA: A lot of lawyers
are not real strong in numbers.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.850
So if you can do both, I
think you have an advantage

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.875
over some of your colleagues.

00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:32.750
JOHN COATES: Walk in
the footsteps of experts

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:37.130
to learn how they use judgment to
answer difficult questions from both

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.260
a financial and a legal perspective.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.110
[MUSIC PLAYING]

